  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Grep each host and confirm the line; record whether a handler instance already exists.</step>
    <step order="2">Pass the four handlers in each host.</step>
    <step order="3">Add one test per host where its package has a jest runner (assert the composer receives the handlers); record hosts without a runner.</step>
    <step order="4">Bump PCF versions and build both PCFs with build:prod.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the tests named in the acceptance criteria, the touched folders' suites, `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` and ESLint on touched files in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components; all pass.</step>
    <step order="6">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` AND this POML's status element to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 -Project spaarke-ontology-platform-r1`.</step>
    <step order="7">Record any deviation from this POML, and the dev-check result, in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/task-188-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a host cannot build the handlers (no Xrm, or no BFF URL), STOP for that host and list it.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Templates and AI in each host">
      <steps>
        <step>Open each host on dev (Compose memo email, a record's Email Members, the Communication page compose, the Communication Actions control)</step>
        <step>Open the template picker, use AI draft, attach a local file</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Template picker, AI sparkle and attachment upload present and working in each; light and dark themed.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Run jest, tsc and ESLint in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components (npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; in a fresh worktree build ../Spaarke.SdapClient and ../Spaarke.Auth first)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/task-188-notes.md</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Each of the four hosts passes onListEmailTemplates, onRenderEmailTemplate, onDraftWithAi and onUploadLocalAttachment from one handler instance (reusing an existing one).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each host with a jest runner has a test that fails without the handlers; hosts without a runner are listed in task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Both PCFs build with build:prod and their versions are bumped in every location.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All existing tests in the touched packages pass; tsc clean in touched files; no new client-lint violations.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
